course: dictionary
lesson: 5716
title: One word, many meanings: look
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word look can mean different things, and the words around it show you which one. «Look at the board» means turn your eyes to see. «You look happy» means you seem happy. The same word does two different jobs.
explain: Look for and look after are phrases. Look for means try to find something: «We had to look for the missing clue.» Look after means take care of someone: «Who will look after the puppy?» Read the words next to look to find which meaning fits.
explain: Look can also be a noun, something you do: «Take a look at this map.» Here a look is an act of looking. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Look is a verb: look, looks, looked, looking.
fact: A look is also a noun: take a look means have a quick view.
fact: «Look» means turn your eyes to see something, or seem: «You look happy.»
fact: «Look for» means try to find, and «look after» means take care of someone.
fact: «Look out!» means be careful, and «look both ways» is a safety rule before you cross a road.
exercise: «At skate parks one rider goes in the bowl at a time, and you look before you drop in.» What does look mean here? | To seem tired | To take care of a friend | To search for a lost shoe | *To turn your eyes and check it is safe first
exercise: «The thylacine looked like a dog.» What does looked mean here? | Took care of | Turned to face the camera | Searched for | *Seemed, or appeared to be
exercise: Nadia says, «Look after your pet.» What does look after mean? | To have a quick glance | To seem happy | To search for a lost pet | *To take care of someone
test: «We had to look for the missing clue.» What does look for mean here? | To take care of | To seem | *To try to find | To be careful
test: «Take a look at this map.» What is a look in this sentence? | A loud noise | A type of hat | A kind of map | *An act of looking, a quick view
exam: «Look out!» shouts Sam as the ball comes towards him. What does look out mean? | Turn your eyes to the window | *Be careful | Take care of the ball | Find the ball
